{"name":"Mr Freeze","hex":"#abd4ec","fetched":"2026-10-23","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Mr Freeze","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of freeze pop, flavored ice or frozen fruit juice in a tube, particularly of the Mr Freeze brand but now also genericized."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Mr_Freeze"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mr. Freeze","blocks":[{"text":"Mr. Freeze is a supervillain appearing in American comic books published by DC Comics. Created by writer Dave Wood and artists Sheldon Moldoff and Bob Kane, the character debuted in Batman #121 as Mr. Zero, a mad scientist with an unknown birth name who, after a physiology-altering mishap, becomes an ice-themed criminal typically armed with freezing weapons and an adversary of the superhero Batman forced to live in sub-zero temperatures and wear a special \"cryo-suit\" for survival. He was later renamed \"Mr. Freeze\" after the version featured in the 1966 Batman television series."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a3/Mr._Freeze_%28Victor_Fries%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mr._Freeze","wikidata":"Q557584"},{"title":"Mr.","blocks":[{"text":"Mister, usually written in its contracted form Mr. or Mr, is a commonly used English honorific for men without a higher honorific, professional title, or any of various designations of office. The title Mr derived from earlier forms of master, as the equivalent female titles Mrs, Miss, and Ms all derived from earlier forms of mistress. Master is sometimes still used as an honorific for boys and young men."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mr.","wikidata":"Q177053"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a3/Mr._Freeze_%28Victor_Fries%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a3/Mr._Freeze_%28Victor_Fries%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMr._Freeze_(Victor_Fries).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d4/Batman121_mr_zero.jpg/250px-Batman121_mr_zero.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d4/Batman121_mr_zero.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d4/Batman121_mr_zero.jpg/250px-Batman121_mr_zero.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" The Pre-Crisis version of Mr. Freeze's first appearance as \"Mr. Zero\" in Batman #121 (February 1959). Art by Curt Swan.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABatman121_mr_zero.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d0/Mr._Freeze_%28New_52%29.jpg/250px-Mr._Freeze_%28New_52%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d0/Mr._Freeze_%28New_52%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d0/Mr._Freeze_%28New_52%29.jpg/250px-Mr._Freeze_%28New_52%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mr. Freeze in Batman Annual (vol. 2) #1 (July 2012). Art by Jason Fabok and Peter Steigerwald.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMr._Freeze_(New_52).jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"The blue of the sky","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/The_blue_of_the_sky.jpg/500px-The_blue_of_the_sky.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_blue_of_the_sky.jpg","share":0.180625},{"title":"Mr. Freeze, Six Flags St. Louis","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/th